# Copy this file to .env and fill it in. .env is never committed. This file holds no values on purpose.
# Check the result with: .venv-desk\Scripts\python check_pipeline.py (Mac: .venv-desk/bin/python check_pipeline.py)

# Required. SEC EDGAR asks every program for a name and an email,
# as in: SEC_USER_AGENT=Your Name your.email@university.edu
SEC_USER_AGENT=

# Required: one model key, and a model of the same provider, written with its CrewAI prefix:
# anthropic/MODEL_ID, gemini/MODEL_ID or openai/MODEL_ID, with a model ID your account can use.
# The agent team and the worksheet both use this pair, and only this pair: the group desk does not read
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY. There is no default model: without MODEL, or with a key and a model of two providers,
# the desk stops at its first step and names the setting. Anthropic has been run end to end; Google AI Studio
# and OpenAI keys go through the same CrewAI calls but have not been run end to end yet.
API_KEY=
MODEL=
# Only for a model server of your own that speaks the OpenAI protocol. Every call of the agent team, with
# API_KEY, then goes to this address instead of the provider's. Leave it out otherwise.
# LLM_BASE_URL=

# Optional: a price, for the P/E and the worksheet's view. Without one, the report has no P/E and the view
# is "not computed". LSEG Workspace must be running and signed in.
# LSEG_APP_KEY=
# Install requirements-lseg.txt in a local .venv-lseg. See docs/lseg-setup.md.
# Automatic: .venv-lseg/bin/python on Mac; .venv-lseg\Scripts\python.exe on Windows.
# Leave this commented out unless you intentionally use another interpreter with the pinned SDK.
# LSEG_PYTHON=
# Or a CSV of closes exported from Workspace (columns ticker, date, close). Keep the file OUTSIDE this folder.
# When it is set, the desk reads it before it asks Workspace. The hit-rate table reads it too.
# LSEG_CLOSES_FILE=
# A ticker's RIC when the desk's reader cannot find it, as JSON: {"TICKER": "RIC"}
# LSEG_RIC_MAP=
# Where the reader notes a request that failed, without prices. Default: closes_diagnostics.jsonl in this
# folder, which git ignores.
# LSEG_DIAGNOSTICS_FILE=

# The AI tools named on the AI-assistance line of each report and of the live record. Default for the
# group desk: Claude Code and OpenAI Codex. Write the tools the team actually used.
# AI_TOOLS=

# The hit-rate table (hit_rate.py) and the base (legacy) desk: team.py, lab03_app.py and lab02_desk.py.
# They read closes through closes.py, whose settings differ from the desk's reader above: a file named by
# CLOSES_FILE (or, when that is absent, LSEG_CLOSES_FILE), and a RIC given as LSEG_RICS=TICKER=RIC,TICKER=RIC.
# LSEG_RIC_MAP is not read there.
# CLOSES_FILE=
# LSEG_RICS=
# LSEG_CLOSE_FIELD=
# The base (legacy) desk only. EFFORT applies to Anthropic models only.
# EFFORT=
# The class key for financialdatasets.ai, the base desk's price source when it has no close.
FINANCIAL_DATASETS_API_KEY=
